  "about": "Signed and hashed statements of parties-identity, computed by generate.py with hashlib and OpenSSL, independently of the Rust code. Binary values are hex; '||' is concatenation. 'handshake' (document 03 section 4): server_proof = Ed25519(server key, 'parties-server-proof-v2' || 00 || exporter); signature = Ed25519(user key, 'parties-auth-v2' || 00 || exporter || server_identity || user_key). 'password': key = Argon2id v1.3 (password UTF-8, salt, memory, passes, lanes, 32 bytes); proof = HMAC-SHA256(key, 'parties-join-pw-v2' || 00 || exporter). 'rotation': signature = Ed25519(old key, 'parties-server-rotation-v1' || 00 || old_key || new_key); statement = old_key || new_key || signature. 'key_link': message = 'parties-link-key-v1' || 00 || exporter || server_identity || account_key || new_key; proof = Ed25519(new key, message); approval = Ed25519(account key, message). 'level': digest = SHA-256('parties-identity-level-v1' || 00 || public_key || counter as 8 bytes little-endian); level = leading zero bits. 'level_search': the smallest counter from 0 that reaches the target.",
